        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The prosecution is simply to prove that the property recovered is stolen property and that the accused extended help in concealment and disposal of the same, as has been held by the Hon'ble Supreme Court of India in the case of Ajendra Nath"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b1bd66d8798c485982bbc0557747db02_25",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is also pertinent to refer to Section 410 of the IPC which reads as under :-\n410. Stolen property.--Property, the possession whereof has been transferred by theft, or by extortion, or by robbery, and property which has been criminally mi"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "698273febf56441693144f709f257bae_26",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "But, if such property subsequently comes into the possession of a person legally entitled to the possession thereof, it then ceases to be stolen property."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5aa473156097484eb0aa79509c94bbde_27",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n(Emphasis supplied) The plain reading of the section 410 of the IPC makes it abundantly clear that the property which has been criminally misappropriated is also a stolen property."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b9c4903234754933b329451ee463451b_28",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "STA"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "9. So far as the offence punishable under Section 379 of the Indian Penal Code is concerned, the essential ingredients to constitute the said offence are:-\n(i) the accused removed the movable property."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "e1ba0efb75c54a6696c76a7ade680eb2_29",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n(ii) he removed it out of the possession of another person without his consent; and (iii) he did so with dishonest intention."
